  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App.tsx Styling**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on `/src/App.tsx`. My current focus is isolating the styling elements as instructed: colors, fonts, spacing, borders, shadows, backgrounds, and gradients. I\'m also examining the layout patterns, specifically flexbox/grid structures and component arrangement within the file.\n\n\n**Refining App.tsx Styling**\n\nI am now carefully reviewing `/src/App.tsx`\'s styling classes, block by block. My focus has shifted to the `Header` section, and specifically the components therein. I am analyzing the existing `flex` properties, `background` colors, and `border` properties, with the goal of matching design requirements. Next I will target the inner elements.\n\n\n**Isolating Header Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the header section styling. I\'m noting the `h-16` height, dark background color, and `text-white` color scheme. The flexbox properties for `items-center` and `justify-between` are important for layout. I\'m taking a close look at the padding and border. The goal is to provide a good start to the professional design theme.\n\n\n**Dissecting Header Components**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the header\'s structure. I\'ve noted the `shadow-lg` and `sticky` properties, as well as the `z-40` value for layering. The `flex items-center gap-3` setup is crucial for the logo and text arrangement. I\'m scrutinizing font sizes, weights, and colors within the nested `div`s, especially the SteelEye title and version info. The goal is to get the component interactions described with precision.\n\n\n**Examining Detail Components**\n\nI\'m now zooming in on the AI Engine status display and the history button within the header. I\'m focusing on their respective flexbox arrangements, especially the `hidden md:flex flex-col items-end` for the AI status, and the `flex items-center gap-3` for the button\'s layout and appearance. I\'m noting the fine details like font sizes (`text-[9px]`, `text-xs`), colors (`text-slate-500`, `text-emerald-400`, `text-slate-200`), and the pulsing animation for the AI status indicator. The button\'s styling, specifically the hover effect, border, and shadow properties are important considerations.\n\n\n**Refining Health Status Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the AI status indicator, specifically the health status display. The design elements I\'m focused on include the small spacing (`gap-1.5`), padding (`px-2.5`, `py-1`), rounded corners, background and border colors, text color, font boldness, and size. The pulsating animation for the health indicator and its conditional background color are also being noted.\n\n\n**Adjusting Sidebar Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the left sidebar panel, specifically the \"\350\275\247\351\222\242\350\257\225\346\240\267\344\270\216\346\235\220\346\226\231\345\275\225\345\205\245\" section. My immediate concern is the visual presentation. The original background is dark. I am considering applying a clean white card style with rounded corners and subtle borders. I will check existing classes to accomplish this.\n\n\n**Revising Main Layout**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the main layout structure and container, specifically within the `/src/App.tsx` file. I\'m focusing on adapting the design from the HTML style guidelines. I\'m considering replacing the existing grid layout with a flexible arrangement, and using card containers for the left and right sections. The goal is to provide a clean and simple white card design for the layout panels. I\'m also ensuring that padding and spacing are consistent with the overall design.\n\n\n**Structuring Column Components**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on restructuring the three-column layout, implementing a new card-based system. The left sidebar will use a white card design with specific styling for a clean look. The center CCD viewer will be a dark display module with precise specifications. The right diagnostics panel will blend white card styling with coil statistics. This system exactly mirrors the HTML structure. Now I\'m preparing to inspect the controls within the Left Sidebar.\n\n\n**Analyzing Sidebar Content**\n\nI am now closely inspecting the sidebar content, starting with the \"\350\275\247\351\222\242\350\257\225\346\240\267\344\270\216\346\235\220\346\226\231\345\275\225\345\205\245\" section. I\'ve noted the blue database icon and text formatting, focusing on the font, color, and spacing. I\'m moving on to the sample presets buttons, considering the layout, text styles, and the count display, especially for the active state. I am considering the use of `space-y-2.5` to accomplish the spacing.\n\n\n**Evaluating Button Interactions**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the button interactions and styles within the sample preset section of the sidebar. I\'m focusing on the conditional styling that is applied, particularly the button\'s background, border, text color, and shadow effects. I\'m noting the use of hover effects and active state variations for visual feedback. The goal is to apply design guidelines, to clarify the interaction model.\n\n\n**Examining Upload Button**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Clear Upload\" button\'s styling. I\'m focusing on the `w-full`, `flex`, `items-center`, `justify-center`, `gap-2`, `py-1.5`, `border`, `bg`, `hover`, and `text` classes. The rounded corners, transition, and text size are important. The objective is to create an appropriate look.\n\n\n\n**Matching CCD Styling**\n\nI\'m now examining the CCD Viewer\'s styling, specifically the middle panel. It exactly mirrors the design guidelines\' inspection visualizer styling: dark background, rounded corners, border, and shadow. I\'m focusing on the `flex` properties, background color, rounded corners, border, and the title bar elements within. I\'m noting the existing layout within the CCD Viewer\'s section.\n\n\n**Refining CCD Viewer Styling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the CCD Viewer\'s header styling, specifically its elements. I\'m noting the dark background, border, and rounded corners, along with the camera icon and text. The goal is to match the HTML design closely, especially the text size, color, and spacing, ensuring consistency. Next I will examine the filter selectors.\n\n\n**Implementing Bottom Controls**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the bottom controls bar beneath the CCD viewer. I\'m adopting the design specified in the HTML guidelines. My aim is to exactly match the existing style, with dark backgrounds, a border, and specific button styling. I will now integrate the new layout.\n\n\n**Matching Bottom Controls**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the CCD overlay and zoom controls at the bottom of the middle panel. I\'m noting the existing button styling with dark backgrounds, text sizes, rounded corners, borders, and hover effects. I\'m focusing on text-slate-500. Then I\'m working to integrate these elements into a clean, intuitive layout, which is consistent with the design guidelines.\n\n\n**Adjusting Right Panel**\n\nI\'m now implementing the right-side panel, adopting a clean, white card style as specified, to contrast with the CCD viewer. I\'m noting the `p-4`, `space-y-4`, `flex flex-col`, `bg-white`, `border`, `rounded-xl`, and `shadow-sm` classes for a clear, modern look. The content header, with icon and text, will have a subtle border. I am carefully integrating the overall rating scorecard with active state highlighting.\n\n\n**Isolating Scorecard Styles**\n\nI am now carefully reviewing the Overall Rating Scorecard section within the right panel. I\'m focusing on the conditional styling based on `overallStatus`, including the background colors, border colors, and text colors (`emerald-850`, `amber-850`, `red-850`). The scorecard will now include a dynamic icon (`ShieldCheck`, `AlertTriangle`, or `ShieldAlert`) and corresponding text (\"\345\220\210\346\240\274\", \"\351\231\215\347\272\247\", \"\344\270\215\345\220\210\346\240\274\"). I am working to ensure consistent visual feedback.\n\n\n**Inspecting Metallurgy Data**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the metallurgy data display within the diagnostics panel. I\'m focusing on the formatting, typography, and conditional background styling, looking at classes like `p-3.5`, `bg-[#151a21]`, `border-[#212c3d]`, and `rounded-xl`. My immediate goal is to match the display with the design guidelines. I\'m noting the existing classes, and I will now make the required adjustments.\n\n\n**Adjusting Panel Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now implementing the design for the micro-mechanics panel. I\'m noting the existing classes, focusing on replacing the dark background with a clean white card style with rounded corners and a subtle border. I am also updating the typography. I am now proceeding to the second panel.\n\n\n**Refining Diagnostics Display**\n\nI am now closely examining the display of \"\345\244\204\347\275\256\346\216\222\344\272\247\346\214\207\344\273\244\345\273\272\350\256\256\". I\'m noting the blue circular indicator, precise text sizes, and font styles. My goal is to ensure this card maintains a clean, modern style consistent with the new card-based layout, and to make it similar to the defect list cards. I am working to ensure that the user can distinguish between the two areas.\n\n\n**Adjusting Defect Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the defect display cards within the right panel, adapting the styling for consistency. I\'m noting the conditional classes for the background, border, and text colors based on severity. The overall status bar at the bottom is being updated with dark backgrounds, a border, and text styles as per the specifications.\n\n\n"
