    thinking: "**Adjusting Canvas Constraints**\n\nI\'m currently focused on responsive canvas sizing. The goal is to make the canvas expand to fill the screen when full-screen mode is active. I plan to modify the `max-h-[500px]` constraint to become either `max-h-full` if full screen, or `h-full` to maximize the height. This seems to be the most streamlined approach.\n\n\n**Refining Size Constraints**\n\nI\'ve been wrestling with aspect ratios and screen sizes. My initial approach using `h-full` and `w-full` introduced some problems with preserving the aspect ratio. Now, I\'m thinking that `max-w-full max-h-full aspect-video` seems better, but I\'m still hitting snags with overflow. Perhaps `max-h-full` with `w-full` is the answer. I might have to rethink how height and width interacts to avoid breaking the aspect ratio, especially on wider displays.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 926228232
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
